[h1]Random New World (RNW)[/h1]

Replace the Americas with a new world for your next EU5 campaign. Sail west into unknown waters, or lead one of its native countries. The Old World stays vanilla.

[h2]🤝 Refined Colonization supported[/h2]
[quote]Compatible with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3816832717]Refined Colonization[/url].
[b]Load order: Refined Colonization → generated RNW world mod.[/b][/quote]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/docs/images/showcase/rnw_showcase_full.gif[/img]

[h2]🌎 A new world to explore[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Six world types:[/b] Supercontinent, continents, small continents, archipelago, scattered islands, or The Wall: a north–south land barrier or island chain with a mountain spine and optional straits.
[*][b]Natural geography:[/b] Branching mountain chains have massifs, passes and foothills. Capes, hooked peninsulas, narrow-mouthed gulfs, inland seas and lagoons give coasts more variety. Lakes have bays, arms and islands, with rivers flowing in and continuing downstream.
[*][b]Room to explore:[/b] The recommended ocean expansion reaches farther across the Pacific. Island groups stay where there is room or move together out of the new continents' way. Sea lanes, currents and crossings follow the geography.
[*][b]Native societies:[/b] Settled countries and decentralized tribes have their own cultures, religions and subject relationships. States grow along coasts, terrain and farming corridors, with stronger cultural and religious cores.
[*][b]Extraordinary peoples:[/b] Optionally add great empires, maritime leagues, highland confederations, fractured realms and sacred centers.
[*][b]Campaign content:[/b] Regional stories, formable countries and colonial names give the new world its own flavor.
[*][b]Keep the surprise:[/b] The map is hidden in country selection and mod thumbnails by default. You can still choose a native country from the list, or reveal the map to inspect it.
[*][b]Make it yours:[/b] Adjust individual resource frequencies, land in native states, peasant share and distance from the Old World. Reroll peoples or resources on the same continent. World Codes preserve your seed and settings.
[*][b]Atlas and queue:[/b] Explore ten map lenses, search places and compare worlds. Choose a continent sketch or queue several worlds, including while another is generating. The generator and world text support all eleven official EU5 languages.
[*][b]Across the Pillars DLC:[/b] Compatible and adapted: New World expeditions and treasure fleets use the generated map. The DLC is optional.
[/list]

[h2]▶ Getting started[/h2]
[quote][b]Enable a generated world in your playset.[/b] This Workshop item carries the generator; each world appears as a separate local mod.[/quote]
[quote][b]RAM warning:[/b] About 7.5 GB of free RAM is needed while generating. With 16 GB of RAM, close EU5 as soon as the generator opens—the game can use nearly all available memory even in the main menu. You can also start the generator directly from the mod folder without opening EU5 at all.[/quote]
[olist]
[*]In EU5’s [b]Mods[/b] menu, find Random New World, click [b]Open in Folder[/b] and launch [b]Random New World Generator[/b].
[*]Choose a world type and settings, or paste a [b]World Code[/b].
[*]Click [b]Generate[/b] and wait a few minutes.
[*]Enable the new world mod, such as [i]RNW: Small continents 7K3Q[/i], and start a new 1337 campaign.
[/olist]

Due to EU5 engine limitations, world generation cannot be integrated directly into the game and must run as a separate application. The generator leaves the game installation untouched, and once created, a world works without it.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/docs/images/proton.png[/img]

The new generator window uses WebView2 on Windows or WebKitGTK 4.1 on native Linux. The classic window opens when these are unavailable, including in EU5’s usual Proton prefix; you can also choose it in Settings.

[h2]ℹ Before you play[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Requirements:[/b] EU5 1.4.6 and about 7.5 GB of free RAM while generating. Other game patches may require a generator update.
[*]Windows: The generator is unsigned. Smart App Control may block it.
[*][b]Saves:[/b] New campaigns only. Keep each save’s original world mod: a newer game or generator may produce a different world from the same code.
[*][b]Switching worlds:[/b] Use one RNW world at a time. Restart EU5 when switching maps.
[*][b]Other mods & multiplayer:[/b] Map overhauls and mods replacing the Americas conflict with RNW. Other mod combinations and multiplayer remain unverified.
[*][b]Ironman & achievements:[/b] Supported under the standard game rules.
[/list]

